{"content":[{"c":["SEPHAR"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Geographical landmark defining one of the boundaries of the territory settled by the sons of Joktan (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.30","r":"Gen.10.30","rawR":"Gen.10.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.30","value":"Gen.10.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:30"},"). Undoubtedly located in southern Arabia, Sephar is most often identified with one of two towns bearing the Arabic name Zafar: the seaport town in central Yemen’s Hadhramaut province, or the site in southern Yemen, once the capital of the Himyarites."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Sephar","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.30","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.30","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.30"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"fb59ecd1f4175c483c441500fc633ec6396f70535322806fd7487f1482e5d3fb","sourceItemName":"Sephar","sourceItemOrder":152,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Sephar","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Sephar","title":"Sephar","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}